Expand gray and palette rows of at most 8 bits to RGBA8 with one routine per row.

spng_decode_scanline() has a row routine for three layouts when the output is
SPNG_FMT_RGBA8: RGBA8 (memcpy), RGB8 (rgb8_row_to_rgba8) and 8-bit palette
(expand_row). Every other layout runs the generic loop, which branches on the
colour type, the depth and the format once per pixel. A gray row of at most 8
bits and a 1, 2 or 4-bit palette row also call get_sample() once per pixel,
and a 1, 2 or 4-bit gray row then takes a second pass through scale_row() and
sample_to_target().

This patch chooses a routine for those rows once, in spng_decode_image(). It
sets the existing `unpack` flag, so the row leaves the loop at the existing
unpack exit, and unpack_scanline() gets the RGBA8 case:

- 1, 2 and 4-bit rows: expand_packed_row() writes 8 pixels per iteration from
  ctx->decode_plte. For a palette image that table already holds the PLTE
  entries with their tRNS alpha. For a gray image the patch fills the first
  2, 4 or 16 entries with the gray ramp: the value that scale_row() gives each
  sample, with alpha 0 for the tRNS sample.
- 8-bit gray and gray+alpha rows: gray8_row_to_rgba8() copies the gray sample
  to the three colours. The alpha is the second sample, or 0 for the tRNS
  sample.

The output is byte for byte what the generic loop writes. That includes the
loop's test of the gray tRNS sample: it compares the whole 16-bit value and
does not mask it to the bit depth, which the PNG specification says a decoder
must do. The ramp and the call of gray8_row_to_rgba8() make the same test. If
one of the three changes, change the others.

SPNG_DECODE_USE_SBIT, every other output format and the 16-bit layouts keep
the generic loop.

unpack_scanline() takes the context as its last parameter. The call in
spng_decode_scanline() then keeps its other arguments in place, and the
compiler emits the same code as before for every other layout (measured: the
same instructions per pixel on x64 and arm64 for Linux, macOS and Windows).
Other ways to reach the routines from that function changed its register
allocation and cost gray and 16-bit rows 1 to 3 instructions per pixel on
some targets.

Upstream: spng.c at master (46c81dc2, 2026-08-31) is the same file as at
v0.7.4 (2023-05-08). There is no upstream issue for this loop.

